{"hasZ":false,"features":[{"attributes":{"gross_square_footage":16537,"project__project_name":"105 Beach Street","last_filed_date":"2026-08-28","sam_ids":null,"latitude":42.35069704,"project_status":"Under Review","project_street_suffix":"Street","description":"The proposed project involves the adaptive reuse of the existing 5-story commercial building located at 105 Beach Street in Boston\u2019s historic Leather District. Currently owned and occupied by Language Studies International (LSI), the building\u2019s upper floors (Floors 2\u20135, totaling 11,334 GFA) will be converted into 15 residential rental apartments. The ground-floor commercial space will retain its long-standing retail tenant, Figaro\u2019s sandwich shop, while repurposing unused ground-floor area into a residential lobby and additional commercial space. The basement level will accommodate secure indoor bicycle storage and mechanical utilities.","project__record_type":"Small Project","total_residential_units":15,"website_url":"https://www.bostonplans.org/projects/development-projects/105-beach-street","project_id":5058,"project_street_number":"105","project_street_name":"Beach","project_zip_code":"02111","last_board_approved_date":null,"neighborhood":"Leather District","objectid":253134,"longitude":-71.05830022},"geometry":{"x":-71.05830022043455,"y":42.35069703961333}},{"attributes":{"gross_square_footage":574000,"project__project_name":"140 Providence Street","last_filed_date":"2026-09-25","sam_ids":"121155","latitude":42.35093775,"project_status":"Under Review","project_street_suffix":"Street","description":"The proposed project would convert the upper floors of the existing building to multifamily residential use, with a total of approximately 476 dwelling units in approximately 503,000 s.f. of GFA, including amenity space newly created in the existing basement. Together, the ground floor and basement would include approximately 41,000 s.f. of retail and restaurant space to activate the Arlington Street, St. James Avenue, and Berkeley Street frontages and reinforce the pedestrian-oriented character of Park Square. Loading from Providence Street would continue, but there are no parking spaces on site and none is proposed.","project__record_type":"Large Project","total_residential_units":476,"website_url":"https://www.bostonplans.org/projects/development-projects/140-providence-street","project_id":5059,"project_street_number":"140","project_street_name":"Providence","project_zip_code":"02116","last_board_approved_date":null,"neighborhood":"Back Bay","objectid":253135,"longitude":-71.07155781},"geometry":{"x":-71.07155781041934,"y":42.35093774991252}},{"attributes":{"gross_square_footage":26680,"project__project_name":"88-91 Commercial Wharf","last_filed_date":"2026-10-01","sam_ids":null,"latitude":42.36152417,"project_status":"Letter of Intent","project_street_suffix":"Row","description":"US Wharf LLC (the Proponent) proposes to demolish the existing structure and construct a new 4-story, 28,680-square-foot boutique hotel containing approximately 35\u201345 keys. The project would also include approximately 2,000 square feet of first-floor restaurant space open to hotel guests and the public, as well as dedicated open space with new Harborwalk connections. As the property is located within the North End Waterfront Sub-District of the Harborpark and exceeds 10,000 square feet of gross floor area, it is subject to Large Project Review.","project__record_type":"Large Project","total_residential_units":null,"website_url":"https://www.bostonplans.org/projects/development-projects/88-91-commercial-wharf","project_id":5068,"project_street_number":"90","project_street_name":"Commercial Wharf East","project_zip_code":"02110","last_board_approved_date":null,"neighborhood":"North End","objectid":253136,"longitude":-71.04935556},"geometry":{"x":-71.04935555963618,"y":42.36152416969173}}],"exceededTransferLimit":false,"hasM":false,"objectIdFieldName":"objectid","field